    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. what about backups though? like, does the company have to go in and wipe every single backup drive and archive, or is there some kind of way around that? it seems like a lot of work to track down every single instance of the data.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "GDPR does not require erasing every single backup, but rather making a 'good-faith' effort to erase personal data from all backup systems. Critical is determining whether the data is considered 'available' (e.g. main data repository, stored data accessible by standard technical means). Apps that automatically prune or delete data periodically aren't considered “systems accessible by data subject-integrated tools.\"",
